[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   step_158: metric-derived TEP slip -- topological winding field (b124).
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   Steps 151/156 inject an *empirical* position slip and measure how it
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   survives the refit chain.  This step derives the slip from a specified
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   matter-metric construction instead of imposing it.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   Field model
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   Matter metric  g~_mn = A^2(phi) g_mn + B(phi) d_m phi d_n phi  with
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   a scalar sector that winds around the boundary axis:
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   phi(x) = m * theta_A(x) * sigma(r)
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   theta_A is the azimuthal angle about the boundary axis A (the
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   resident axis 49 deg, -17 deg), rho_A the cylindrical distance to
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   the axis, and sigma(r) a radial envelope that switches the winding
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   sector on inside the boundary radius r_b (logistic, width w).
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   To first order in B the matter-frame proper-time rate acquires
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   kappa (u . grad phi), so a comet accumulates
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   dt = kappa * int (v . grad phi) dt
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   = kappa m [ int sigma(r) dtheta  +  int theta d sigma ]
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   |__ non-integrable winding __|   |__ integrable part __|
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   The second term is single-valued: for a transit in and back out it
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   contributes only boundary values of theta*sigma and is the analogue
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   of oint d ln A = 0 -- a coherent offset that the step_151 control
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   already showed reads back invisible through refits.  The first term
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   is the holonomy: it counts the winding the trajectory executes
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   about the axis inside the boundary and survives as an
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   equivalent-time offset -> position slip delta x = v_hat * c * dt,
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   the same channel step_151 showed propagates to a fitted
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   inbound-asymptote displacement.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   Predictions derived from the construction (not fitted per-observable):
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   * per-comet slip amplitude proportional to the boundary-weighted
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   winding W_in = int sigma theta_dot dt  (non-integrable);
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   * flat response in crossing velocity (holonomy, not impulse --
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   the step_145 discriminator);
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   * axis specificity: a control axis placed away from (49,-17)
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   must destroy the correlation with the measured slips;
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   * shell-resolved accumulation profile: where in radius the
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   winding accrues.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   Implementation
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   For each comet of the dual-leg cohort (step_b91 refits) the true
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   SBDB orbit is marched backward (inbound history) and forward
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   (outbound future) to 250 AU with Sun+planets (IAS15, same boundary
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   integrator as step_155).  Along each step the azimuth increment
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   about A is accumulated with weight sigma(r) -> W_in, W_out, and the
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   integrable gauge term G = int theta dsigma.  dt_pred = kappa m W_in
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   with kappa m calibrated once on the cohort median |our_dtau|.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   Tests
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T1  Spearman(dt_pred, our_dtau) over the cohort.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T2  Mann-Whitney |W_in| in-cap vs out-of-cap (axis-specificity of
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   the predicted partition).
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T3  corr(dt_pred, v_cross) vs the impulse-model expectation
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   (dt ~ 1/v): holonomy flatness.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T4  control axes: same W_in statistic evaluated about 4 axes at
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   ~90-180 deg from the resident axis -- the correlation must
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   collapse if the field is really anchored on (49,-17).
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T5  shell decomposition of W_in (cumulative winding vs radius).
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T6  integrable-part bookkeeping: |G_in + G_out| vs |W_in + W_out|.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T7  boundary-radius sensitivity: W_in recomputed for
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   r_b in {50,100,150,250} -- which envelope best tracks the
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   measured slips.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T8  axis-threading analysis: rho_min (closest approach of the
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   trajectory to the axis line) vs |dtau|, raw and
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   q-partialled, on the resident and control axes -- the control
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   axes expose whether rho_min is axis physics or a perihelion-
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   distance proxy.
[2026-09-21 15:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 158]   T9  signed winding vs signed measured rotation.
